# 27B environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in a key to enable the imagery renderer.
# Everything EXCEPT the final 3D render (geocoding, building/height lookup,
# elevation + heading math, caching, metrics, and the full UI) works with no
# key. With no key set, the app shows the honest "imagery source not configured"
# state — never a placeholder or simulated scene.

# Google Maps Platform API key with the "Map Tiles API" enabled
# (Photorealistic 3D Tiles). This gates the CesiumJS renderer.
#
# Get one at https://console.cloud.google.com/ -> APIs & Services -> Credentials,
# then enable "Map Tiles API". Restrict the key to your deploy origin(s).
#
# COST NOTE (updated 2026-08-04 per the real-imagery feasibility proof --
# see docs/repair/product-proof-sprint/27b/REPORT.md): billing is per ROOT
# TILESET REQUEST, not per tile -- one root request buys the whole renderer
# session (at least 3 hours of unmetered tile requests within it), so cost
# scales as ~1 billable event per render, not per tile. Free to 1,000
# root-tileset requests/month, then ~$6/1,000 -- roughly 1,000 free renders/
# month, not per address. Google's Map Tiles terms PROHIBIT caching this
# imagery (Maps Platform ToS section 3.2.3(b)), so the app deliberately does
# NOT cache renders -- every visit to the same address is a new billable
# event. Do NOT exceed the free cap in production without an explicit cost
# decision, and set a daily quota cap in the Cloud console before any public
# deploy.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=
